      "sut_name": "burgers-1d",
      "display_name": "1D Burgers — ScaleInitial (amplitude → peak monotone)",
      "description": "Amplitude-monotonicity MP_mono: the inviscid Burgers equation u_t + (u²/2)_x = 0 is nonlinear, but strictly-positive scaling of the initial Gaussian pulse must strictly increase the final peak amplitude. Lax-Friedrichs is dissipative (peak ratio < 2 due to shock smearing), so the assertion is GreaterThan rather than equal scaling.",
